WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.033 --> 00:00:02.367
-Welcome, welcome, welcome to

00:00:02.367 --> 00:00:03.734
"The Tonight Show," everybody.

00:00:03.734 --> 00:00:05.501
You're here.
Thank you for watching.

00:00:05.501 --> 00:00:07.434
[ Cheers and applause ]
I appreciate it.

00:00:07.434 --> 00:00:09.100
Let's get to some news, guys.

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:12.267
President Biden's approval
rating continues to slide.

00:00:12.267 --> 00:00:13.601
Yeah. And a new poll found that
since taking office,

00:00:13.601 --> 00:00:18.133
the biggest drop in support has
been among young voters.

00:00:18.133 --> 00:00:19.834
Yeah. Though, to Biden,
I'm pretty sure

00:00:19.834 --> 00:00:22.601
a young voter is just a voter.

00:00:24.834 --> 00:00:26.133
Then Biden said,

00:00:26.133 --> 00:00:27.801
"So this means I'm doing okay
with older voters?"

00:00:27.801 --> 00:00:31.634
And his staff was like,
"Oh, goodness no, no."

00:00:31.634 --> 00:00:32.834
Speaking of Biden, I read,

00:00:32.834 --> 00:00:35.000
as fuel prices
continue to surge,

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:37.834
The White House is considering
a temporary suspension

00:00:37.834 --> 00:00:39.901
of the federal gas tax.

00:00:39.901 --> 00:00:44.434
Yeah, they're
considering it, so...

00:00:44.434 --> 00:00:46.200
take your time, gang.

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:49.467
You can tell president is on
the older side when he's like,

00:00:49.467 --> 00:00:51.834
"What if we give everyone
a quarter?"

00:00:55.801 --> 00:00:57.868
Yep, the economy has
really been struggling lately.

00:00:57.868 --> 00:01:00.734
I saw that the stock market is
now in its biggest free fall

00:01:00.734 --> 00:01:02.601
since the start of the pandemic.

00:01:02.601 --> 00:01:05.267
Right now, the ticker on CNBC is
just showing the lyrics to

00:01:05.267 --> 00:01:07.167
"Everybody Hurts."

00:01:09.033 --> 00:01:10.501
Meanwhile,
since stocks are all down,

00:01:10.501 --> 00:01:13.934
I saw that CNN suggested
investing in baseball cards.

00:01:13.934 --> 00:01:15.601
Did you hear this?

00:01:15.601 --> 00:01:17.467
Yeah. I guess their
chief financial strategist

00:01:17.467 --> 00:01:21.033
is a 10-year-old from 1986.

00:01:21.033 --> 00:01:22.767
Then, to battle
rising food prices,

00:01:22.767 --> 00:01:24.100
they recommend eating
the gum inside

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:25.133
the pack of baseball cards.

00:01:25.133 --> 00:01:26.300
Hey, get this.

00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:28.701
A new study found that
staring at yourself

00:01:28.701 --> 00:01:31.868
during Zoom calls
can put you in a bad mood.

00:01:31.868 --> 00:01:34.601
[ Laughter ]

00:01:34.601 --> 00:01:37.300
You know what else about Zoom
calls put you in a bad mood?

00:01:37.300 --> 00:01:39.868
Being on Zoom calls. Yeah.

00:01:40.334 --> 00:01:42.033
Yeah, it's better to
stare at your co-worker

00:01:42.033 --> 00:01:45.400
who thinks a Zoom call is the
ideal time to eat Greek yogurt.

00:01:46.033 --> 00:01:49.601
You think the visual is bad,
the audio -- Just mute yourself.

00:01:49.601 --> 00:01:51.667
Hey, I want to say
congrats to Post Malone,

00:01:51.667 --> 00:01:53.734
who just welcomed
a new baby girl.

00:01:53.734 --> 00:01:55.968
[ Cheers and applause ]
Post!

00:01:55.968 --> 00:01:57.701
Congrats.

00:02:01.467 --> 00:02:02.767
Yep.

00:02:02.767 --> 00:02:05.367
We've actually got
a picture of her right here.

00:02:05.367 --> 00:02:06.868
-Stop!

00:02:06.868 --> 00:02:08.234
♪♪

00:02:08.234 --> 00:02:11.400
♪ Don't do it, Jimmy ♪

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:15.100
♪ Don't bring
yourself disgrace ♪

00:02:15.100 --> 00:02:17.667
♪ Don't show a baby ♪

00:02:17.667 --> 00:02:23.234
♪ With tattoos
Photoshopped on its face ♪

00:02:23.234 --> 00:02:25.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:28.734 --> 00:02:30.100
-But I wanna.

00:02:30.100 --> 00:02:31.734
♪♪

00:02:31.734 --> 00:02:35.000
-♪ Don't do this, Jimmy ♪

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:38.901
♪ Have you no self-esteem? ♪

00:02:38.901 --> 00:02:41.667
♪ That joke's too easy ♪

00:02:41.667 --> 00:02:47.000
♪ Open your mind and dream ♪

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:48.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:52.834 --> 00:02:54.901
-But we -- we already
made the graphic.

00:02:54.901 --> 00:02:56.000
♪♪

00:02:56.000 --> 00:03:00.133
-♪ Oh, simple Jimmy ♪

00:03:00.133 --> 00:03:03.801
♪ Heed my words, hear my cry ♪

00:03:03.801 --> 00:03:06.868
♪ You're better than this joke ♪

00:03:06.868 --> 00:03:12.100
♪ Now spread your wings
and fly ♪

00:03:12.100 --> 00:03:14.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:18.534 --> 00:03:19.567
-Are you done?

00:03:19.567 --> 00:03:21.801
-Yeah, yeah. Pretty much.
-Okay.

00:03:21.801 --> 00:03:24.334
Well, anyway,
here's Post Malone's baby.

00:03:24.334 --> 00:03:27.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:27.167 --> 00:03:29.067
-[ Laughing ] Damn!

00:03:29.067 --> 00:03:31.634
Alright. Alright.
That -- that's cool.

00:03:31.634 --> 00:03:33.067
-That's not bad.

00:03:33.067 --> 00:03:34.868
Tariq Trotter, ladies and
gentlemen, right there.

00:03:34.868 --> 00:03:36.534
That's not bad.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:41.033 --> 00:03:44.234
I don't know if you guys saw
this, but earlier this morning,

00:03:44.234 --> 00:03:46.801
one of our local NBC anchors,
Michael Gargiulo,

00:03:46.801 --> 00:03:48.067
had a little trouble
getting through

00:03:48.067 --> 00:03:49.334
the traffic report.

00:03:49.334 --> 00:03:50.801
And we thought we would be nice

00:03:50.801 --> 00:03:52.634
